# Architecture rules (ALWAYS APPLY)

## Monorepo layout

This is a pnpm + Turborepo monorepo. Layout is fixed:

```
apps/
  api/              # Hono API — the ONLY place that touches the DB directly
  admin-web/        # TanStack Start — admin panel only
  internal-web/     # TanStack Start — employees + viewers
  portal-web/       # TanStack Start — clients
packages/
  db/               # Drizzle schema + migrations + client + seeds
  shared/           # Zod schemas, types, enums, permissions, constants, pure utils
  auth/             # Better-Auth config + permission resolver
  excel/            # ExcelJS import/export logic
  i18n/             # Paraglide-generated translations
  ui/               # Shared React components (shadcn base layer)
  logger/           # Pino setup
```

### Dependency direction (STRICT, no exceptions)

- `apps/*` may depend on `packages/*`
- `packages/*` may NEVER depend on `apps/*`
- `packages/db` depends only on `packages/shared`
- No circular dependencies — ever. CI enforces this.

If you need shared logic between two apps, put it in `packages/shared`. If you're
tempted to import from `apps/api` inside `apps/admin-web`, you're doing it wrong.

## Module anatomy (mandatory for every API module)

Every module under `apps/api/src/modules/<name>/` has:

```
<name>.schema.ts         # Re-exports from packages/db
<name>.validators.ts     # Zod schemas for inputs
<name>.repository.ts     # Data access only; no business logic
<name>.service.ts        # Business logic; orchestrates repo, emits events, audit
<name>.controller.ts     # HTTP adapter; thin; parses, calls service, formats response
<name>.routes.ts         # Route registration with permission middleware
<name>.types.ts          # Module-internal types (optional)
__tests__/               # Tests for everything in the module
```

**DO NOT** collapse service + controller into one file. **DO NOT** skip validators.

## Layer responsibilities (STRICT)

| Layer | May do | May NOT do |
|---|---|---|
| Controller | Parse request, call service, format response | Call DB, implement business logic |
| Service | Business logic, call repositories, emit events, audit log | Touch HTTP Context, read req headers |
| Repository | Run DB queries, return plain objects, throw domain errors | Implement business logic, call other services |

A controller that calls `db.select(...)` directly is a bug. Always go through the service → repository chain.

## HTTP types stay in controllers

`service.ts` and `repository.ts` must never import from `hono` or any HTTP-related module.
They work with plain objects. This means services are easy to unit-test and easy to reuse (e.g., from a CLI script).

## Three frontends, one API

Never add admin-only endpoints to internal-web or vice versa.
Protection is done via `requirePermission('…')` middleware on every route.

The frontends proxy `/api/*` to the API via Railway's private network. Client-side code
calls `/api/...` as same-origin — it never talks to `api.mrengines.rs` directly.

## Subdomain isolation

Admin, internal, and portal are **physically separate apps**. Never import UI
components between them. Shared components live in `packages/ui`.

Cookies are host-only (NOT cross-subdomain). A user authenticated on internal-web
is NOT automatically authenticated on admin-web. This is intentional.

## Dependency injection

All services and repositories are instantiated in `apps/api/src/core/container.ts`.
Never use module-level singletons or imported globals for stateful things.

Tests build a container with fakes/stubs as needed. Production code never reaches into
the container directly — it receives dependencies via constructor.

## Events and real-time

Cross-module notifications use the in-process `EventBus` (apps/api/src/modules/events/event-bus.ts).
Services emit events; other services (or the SSE hub) subscribe.

Never send a SSE event directly from a controller. Always go through the service.

## Migrations

- Database migrations live in `packages/db/migrations/`
- Generated via `drizzle-kit generate`
- Forward-only. To revert, write a new migration. Never rollback DB in production.
- Every PR that changes `packages/db/src/schema/*` MUST include a migration file.

## No magic paths

- All file paths are constructed via utilities in `apps/api/src/infrastructure/storage/`
- All URLs constructed via helpers, not string concatenation
- All env vars read via a single validated `env.ts` using Zod

If you see `process.env.FOO` outside `core/config/env.ts`, that's a bug.

## Testing is not optional

Every new module ships with tests. Coverage thresholds (per `docs/10-testing.md`)
are CI-enforced. A feature is "done" when tests pass and coverage holds.

## Read before coding

Before starting any task, read:
- docs/04-modules.md (if working on structure)
- docs/02-data-model.md (if touching schema)
- docs/03-permissions.md (if touching auth/access)
- docs/10-testing.md (always)
- This rule file + any others that apply

Ask Nikola if anything conflicts.
